  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTION AND CONSERVATION OF WESTERN CHIMPANZEES IN THE HAUT NIGER NATIONAL PARK, GUINEA.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO REDUCE THE RAPID INCREASE OF THREATS TO WESTERN CHIMPANZEE POPULATIONS AND OTHER BIODIVERSITY IN HAUT NIGER NATIONAL PARK, GUINEA BY (1) PROTECTING RELEASED AND FREE-RANGING CHIMPANZEES, AND MINIMIZING HUMAN-CHIMPANZEE CONTACT, THROUGH PHYSICAL STAFF PRESENCE AND ACTIVE MONITORING (2) EXPANDING AN ONGOING CAMERA TRAP PROJECT TO COVER 100% OF THE PARK S MAFOU CORE AREA (3) INCREASING AWARENESS AND SUPPORT FOR CHIMPANZEE CONSERVATION BY DISSEMINATING CAMERA TRAP DATA IN SCIENTIFIC PUBLICATIONS AND TO LOCAL COMMUNITIES, EXPANDING THE EDUCATION FOR CONSERVATION PROGRAM, AND AIRING EDUCATIONAL PROGRAMMING ON LOCAL RADIO (4) REDUCING ANTHROPOGENIC PRESSURES ON THE PARK BY APPLYING RESULTS OF A SOCIOECONOMIC STUDY TO GUIDE DEVELOPMENT OF ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS ACTIVITIES, SUCH AS BEEKEEPING.</narrative>
  </description>
